A tool call without await in the async dialect yields a promise, not the value.
-- script.js --
const first = await mcp.crm.get({id: 1});
const second = mcp.crm.get({id: 2});
try { return [first.args.id, second.args === undefined, typeof second]; } catch (e) { return e.message; }
-- tools.json --
{
  "crm.get": null
}
-- divergence --
Async dialect: tool calls return values, so a call without await is already the result rather than a Promise.
